  "scopeNotes": [
    "Physical and logical cat gates use analytical SDK error models, not bosonic Fock-space dynamics. Adapter currently measures in the encoded computational/Z basis only.",
    "Pulser public C6 and reported amplitudes were independently compared to a dense Hamiltonian including phase and asymmetric three-atom interactions. Differences of approximately 3.5e-4 to 4.4e-4 against an ideal continuous constant pulse are attributable to the explicitly documented nanosecond sampling/terminal zero interpolation; solver tolerance is not a bound on that model discretization.",
    "QoolQit uses actual compilation, and independent checks verified TIME*ENERGY=1000 and DISTANCE^6*ENERGY=C6 as well as equivalence to separately built physical Pulser inputs.",
    "IQM local transpilation and validation are real SDK operations. Three fake targets were tested with a routed reverse-control/swap circuit; compiled measurements preserve logical classical-bit identity. Static readout noise and seeded Aer replay were verified."
  ],
  "independentCheckCount": 26,
  "hashScope": "Frozen implementation, contracts, numerical tests and dependency locks. Documentation and later Harness/live test additions are outside this implementation hash snapshot."
}
